                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to B String
                to a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fivebrane+structure"} fivebrane structure
                is the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/second+fractional+Pontryagin+class"} second fractional Pontryagin class
          %h4#NecessityOfSmoothRefinement Necessity of smooth refinement
          %p
            We will below consider a
            %em smooth refinement
            of the above Whitehead tower. Before we do so, here a few words on why we need to do this.
          %p One way to state the general problem is:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  The
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
                  of, say, the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+group"} spin group
                  is
                  %strong not
                  a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fine+moduli+space"} fine moduli space
                %em .
              %p
                Because, while homotopy classes
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Maps
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mi Spin
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∼
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Maps(X, B Spin)_\sim
                of maps
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                      %mi Spin
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to B Spin
                are in bijection with equivalence classes of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+bundles"} spin bundles
                on
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Maps
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi B
                      %mi Spin
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∼
                      %mo =
                      %mi Maps
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Spin
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∼
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Maps(X, \Omega B Spin)_\sim = Maps(X, Spin)_\sim
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopies"} homotopies
                from the trivial map
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mo *
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                      %mi Spin
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to * \to B Spin
                are
                %em not
                in general in bijection with the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformations"} gauge transformations
                of the trivial spin bundle: the latter form the set of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Spin
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X,Spin)
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Maps
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∼
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Maps(X, B(-))_\sim
                does not give the right
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BRST-complex"} BRST-complex
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge theory
                in terms of just bare (as opposed to geometric)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
                does not yield an admissible starting point for
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
                (by
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+formalism"} BV-BRST formalism
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Maps
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∼
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Maps(X, B(-))_\sim
                cannot distinguish a group from its
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+compact+subgroup"} maximal compact subgroup
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi O
                        %mo ↪
                        %msub
                          %mi GL
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O \hookrightarrow GL_n
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vielbeins"} vielbeins
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+vielbeins"} generalized vielbeins
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exceptional+generalized+geometry"} exceptional generalized geometry
          %p
            in terms of classifying spaces the entire discussion
            %a{:href => "#VielbeinFields"} of vielbein fields above
            would collapse;
          %p
            higher analogs of this problem include for instance that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Maps
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∼
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Maps(X, B(-))_\sim
            cannot distinguish over 10-dimensional spacetime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            an
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E8"} E8
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+field"} gauge field
            from a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NS5-brane"} NS5-brane
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/magnetic+charge"} magnetic charge
          %ol
            %li
              eventually an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
              on the space of fields is to be constructed as a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+section"} flat section
              of a smooth
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle+with+connection"} circle bundle with connection
              on the space of fields – which requires some smooth structure on that space.
          %p
            These problems are all fixed by refining
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+spaces"} classifying spaces
            such as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo ∈
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B Spin \in \infty Grpd
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-groupoid"} smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stacks"} moduli stacks
            such as
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Smooth
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B} Spin \in Smooth \infty Grpd
          %h4#SmoothRefinement Smooth refinement
          %p
            We considered
            %a{:href => "#SmoothModuliStacks"} above
            the smooth refinement of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B G
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-groupoid"} smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/obstruction"} obstruction
            theory. The problem is that a smooth stack is necessarily a smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+n-type"} homotopy 1-type
            (even if its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
            is a higher type! see below), while the higher stages of the smooth Whitehead tower need to be smooth
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+n-types"} homotopy n-types
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-groupoids"} n-groupoids
            for higher
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            But there is an evident refinement of the above discussion to such
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                smooth
                = succeed "-types" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            To that end we first need a good model for bare homotopy types. One observes that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            functor embeds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
            into
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complexes"} Kan
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coskeleton"} 2-coskeletal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            which is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coskeleton"} (n+1)-coskeletal
            may be regarded as an
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-groupoid"} n-groupoid
            modelling a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+n-type"} homotopy n-type
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi Groupoids
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↙
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo ↘
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi N
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Categories
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi KanComplexes
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mi N
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↙
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi QuasiCategories
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi SimplicialSets
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; Groupoids
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{N}}
                  \\\
                  Categories &amp;&amp;&amp; &amp; KanComplexes
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{N}}\searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; QuasiCategories
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; SimplicialSets
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            A morphism between groupoids
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Y
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+groupoids"} equivalence of groupoids
            precisely if it is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+surjective+functor"} essentially surjective functor
            and a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            classes / connected components, and on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+groups"} automorphism groups
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1
          %p
            Accordingly, we say that a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
            between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complexes"} Kan complexes
            is a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Y
            which induces an isomorphism on all
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
            if it induces such isomorphisms.
          %p Write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Groupoids
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi SimplicialSets
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi weak
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi homotopy
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi equivalences
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\infty Groupoids \simeq SimplicialSets[ \{ weak\;homotopy\;equivalences\}^{-1} ]
          %p
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            obtained by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+localization"} localization
            at the weak homotopy equivalences:
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} ∞-groupoids
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            defines a Kan complex/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+simplicial+complex"} singular simplicial complex
            construction
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sing
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sing X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+hypothesis"} equivalence between
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            of topological spaces and simplicial sets
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Top
                  %mover
                    %munderover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi Sing
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mo −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi sSet
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Top
                  \\stackrel{\stackrel{{\vert-\vert}}{\leftarrow}}{
                  \\underoverset{\simeq}{Sing}{\to}
                  }
                  sSet
                  \\,.
          %p
            In view of this, the
            %a{:href => "#WhiteheadTower"} above
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead+tower"} Whitehead tower
            can be understood entirely as taking place in Kan complexes.
          %p
            For instance for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-groupoid"} 2-groupoid
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 2
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi disc
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ⇓
                              %mrow
                                %mi a
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi A
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                    %mo }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{B}^2 U(1)_{disc}
                  \=
                  \\left\{
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; \to
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \nearrow &amp;&amp; \searrow
                  \\\
                  *
                  \&amp;&amp;\Downarrow^{a \in A}&amp;&amp;
                  *
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \searrow &amp;&amp; \nearrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \to
                  }
                  \\right\}
          %p
            corresponds to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+space"} Eilenberg-MacLane space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(A,2)
          %p
            More generally, for each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\bullet
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
            provides a Kan complex
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ξ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Xi(A_\bullet)
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+homotopy+groups"} simplicial homotopy groups
            are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+homology"} chain homology
            groups of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\bullet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mo •
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\bullet \to B_\bullet
            is sent to a weak homotopy equivalence
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ξ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ξ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Xi(A_\bullet) \to \Xi(B_\bullet)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-abelian+cohomology"} non-abelian
            generalization of chain complexes with quasi-isomorphisms inverted.
          %p
            Using this, we can easily state the generalization of the definition of smooth stacks from above: we obtain a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} smooth ∞-stacks
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo ≔
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H} \coloneqq
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
            by considering simplicial sets parameterized over smooth manifolds and forcing
            = succeed "wise" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"} stalk
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
