                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tfrac{1}{6}\mathbf{p}_2 \simeq \exp(\mu_7)
                is the Lie integration of a canonical 7-cocycle
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %msub
                        %mi μ
                        %mn 7
                      %mo :
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi 𝔰𝔱𝔯𝔦𝔫𝔤
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mn 7
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}\mu_7 : \mathbf{B}\mathfrak{string} \to \mathbf{B}^7 \mathbb{R}
                (
                %a{:href => "#FSSa"}> FSSa
                ).
          %h4#DifferentialRefinement Differential refinement
          %p
            While the
            %a{:href => "#SmoothWhitehead"} above
            smooth refinement of the Whitehead tower already improves on the
            %a{:href => "#WhiteheadTower"} bare Whitehead tower
            by remembering the correct spaces of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformations"} gauge transformations
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instanton"} instanton
            sectors” of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fields"} gauge fields
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+fields"} higher gauge fields
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundles"} principal ∞-bundles
            %em smooth cohomology
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
            such as to encode the actual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+fields"} higher gauge fields
            themselves. This differential cohomology in turn is naturally available in terms of
            %em curvature twisted flat cohomology
            or equivalently
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                curvature-twisted
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+systems"} local systems
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p In order to get a feeling for what differential refinements of higher moduli stacks are going to be like, recall two structures that we have already seen above:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
                the smooth moduli stack of smooth
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connections"} principal connections
                from
                %a{:href => "#SpinConnection"} above
                is presented by
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mi conn
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mover
                        %munder
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mrow
                        %mo {
                        %mi A
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi g
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mi A
                        %mi g
                        %mo +
                        %msup
                          %mi g
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mi d
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi A
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo ,
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mi g
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo ,
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo }
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\mathbf{B}G_{conn}
                      \=
                      (C^\infty(-,G) \times \Omega^1(-, \mathfrak{g})
                      \\stackrel{\overset{}{\to}}{\underset{}{\to}}
                      \\Omega^1(-, \mathfrak{g}))
                      \=
                      \\left\{
                      A \stackrel{g}{\to} (g^{-1} A g + g^{-1} d g)
                      |
                      A \in \Omega^1(-,\mathfrak{g}),
                      g \in C^\infty(-,G)
                      \\right\}
                      \\,.
              %p
                In the special case that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mo =
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G = U(1)
                is abelian, this is the image under the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
                of the length 1 complex of sheaves of abelian groups
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi conn
