          %h3#Anomalies
            %strong Interlude)
            Anomaly line bundle on smooth moduli stacks of fields
          %p
            Before coming to the description in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+%E2%88%9E-stacks"} moduli ∞-stacks
            below, we make some introductory comments on the general origin of twisted differential structures in higher gauge theory, following (
            %a{:href => "#Freed"}> Freed
            ). We add some stacky aspects to that and explain why.
          %p
            In summary, we discuss how the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            of higher gauge theory in the presence of electric and magnetic charge is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle+with+connection"} circle bundle with connection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
