                      \\phi_{ga} : X \to \mathbf{B} E_8
              %p
                and these fields must satisfy what in string theory literature is called the
                = succeed "," do
                  %em flux quantization condition
                %a{:href => "#HopkinsSinger"} Hopkins-Singer 05
                is called an
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+integral+Wu+structure"} differential integral Wu structure
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mn 2
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mi gr
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo +
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mn 2
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mi ga
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi H
                        %mn 4
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      [\phi_C]
                      \=
                      [\frac{1}{2}p_1(\phi_{gr})]
                      +
                      [2\mathbf{a}(\phi_{ga})]
                      \\;\;
                      \\in H^4(X, \mathbb{Z})
                      \\,.
          %p
            (Depending on convention one may write “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 \phi_C
            ” for “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_C
            ” here, regarding the physical
            = succeed "-field" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 3
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to \mathbf{B}^3 U(1)_conn
            above, see the remark
            %a{:href => "arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/9609122v2.pdf#page=2"} below (1.2)
            in
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Witten
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9609122"} arXiv:hep-th/9609122
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+infinity-groupoid"} discrete
            1-groupoid model satisfying these points has been by
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Freed"} Freed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Greg+Moore"} Moore
            and others (see the references
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "supergravity+C-field#References"} here
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+homotopy+type+theory"} cohesive homotopy type theory
            and following (
            %a{:href => "#FSSc"}> FSSc
            ) we now obtain naturally a genuine
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+infinity-stack"} smooth moduli 3-stack
            of such field configurations: the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} interpretation
            of the evident expression
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi CField
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi gr
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi ga
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi p
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi gr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mn 2
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi ga
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi C
                    %mo }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{CField}(X)
                  \\coloneqq
                  \\left\{
                  \\phi_{gr}, \phi_{ga}, \phi_{C}
                  |
                  \\frac{1}{2}\mathbf{p}_1(\phi_{gr})
                  +
                  2\mathbf{a}(\phi_{ga})
                  \\simeq
                  \\phi_C
                  \\right\}
          %p
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            is (see
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HoTT+methods+for+homotopy+theorists"} HoTT methods for homotopy theorists
            for how this works) the smooth
            = succeed "-stack" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi CField
                  %mo ∈
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{CField} \in \mathbf{H}
            given as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi CField
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %msub
                            %mi Spin
                            %mi conn
                          %mo ×
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %msub
                            %mi E
                            %mn 8
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ⇙
                            %mo ≃
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mrow
                              %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                                %mfrac
                                  %mn 1
                                  %mn 2
                              %msub
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi p
                                %mn 1
                              %mo +
                              %mn 2
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi a
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mn 3
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi conn
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mn 3
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathbf{CField} &amp;\to&amp; \mathbf{B} Spin_{conn} \times \mathbf{B}E_8
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;\swArrow_{\simeq}&amp; \downarrow^{\tfrac{1}{2}\mathbf{p}_1 + 2\mathbf{a}}
                  \\\
                  \\mathbf{B}^3 U(1)_{conn} &amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp; \mathbf{B}^3 U(1)
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            On the right this has the universal local coefficient bundle for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi String
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{String}^{2\mathbf{a}}
            from
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#HigherUnitaryTwistedCovers"} above
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} C-field
            configuration as being (a partial differential refinement of) a
            = succeed "-twisted" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\phi_C]
            = succeed "-structure." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi String
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} String^{2\mathbf{a}}
          %h4#TwistedStringStructure
            %strong c)
            Twisted differential String-structure – Green-Schwarz mechanism
          %p
            By
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ho%C5%99ava-Witten+theory"} Hořava-Witten theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string"} heterotic string
            may be understood as being a boundary (or rather
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
            fixed points, see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#HWCompactifications"} below
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11d SuGra
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
                4-form
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mn 4
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_4(\phi_C)
                vanishes;
            %li
              %p
                and the
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mn 8
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_8
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
                picks up a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection
          %p
            This means that the
            %a{:href => "#SuGraFluxQuantization"} above
            defining homotopy pullback for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi CField
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{CField}
            goes over into the one that defines the differential refinement
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi String
                    %mrow
                      %mi conn
                      %mo ′
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} String^{\mathbf{a}}_{conn'}
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi String
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} String^{\mathbf{a}}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %msubsup
                            %mi String
                            %mrow
                              %mi conn
                              %mo ′
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi a
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %msub
                            %mi Spin
                            %mi conn
                          %mo ×
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi E
                            %mn 8
                          %mo ×
                          %msub
                            %mi E
                            %mn 8
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi conn
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi ϕ
                                  %mi B
                          %msub
                            %mo ⇙
                            %mo ≃
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mrow
                              %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                                %mfrac
                                  %mn 1
                                  %mn 2
                              %msub
                                %mover
                                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                    %mi p
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                                %mn 1
                              %mo +
                              %mover
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi a
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Ω
                            %mi cl
                            %mn 3
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ↪
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi ϕ
                                %mi C
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mn 3
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi conn
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathbf{B}String^{\mathbf{a}}_{conn'}
                  \&amp;\to&amp;
                  \\mathbf{B} Spin_{conn} \times \mathbf{B}(E_8 \times E_8)_{conn}
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;{}^{\mathllap{\phi_B}}\swArrow_{\simeq}&amp;
                  \\downarrow^{\tfrac{1}{2}\hat \mathbf{p}_1  + \hat \mathbf{a}}
                  \\\
                  \\Omega^3_{cl}(-) &amp; \stackrel{\phi_C}{\hookrightarrow} &amp; \mathbf{B}^3 U(1)_{conn}
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p On cohomology classes this means that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi gr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi ga
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [\tfrac{1}{2}p_1(\phi_{gr})] = [a(\phi_{ga})] \;\; \in H^4(X, \mathbb{Z})
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is the integral part of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+mechanism"} Green-Schwarz mechanism
            for the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string
          %p
            Since this is now refined not just to cocycles, but to differential cocycles – to
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} String
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{String}^{\mathbf{a}}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+2-bundle"} 2-connections
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to X\}
          %p
            A morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %msubsup
                    %mi String
                    %mi conn
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to String^{2\mathbf{a}}_{conn}
            classifies field content that is expressed with respect to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/good+open+cover"} good open cover
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to X\}
            in particular over single patches
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
            by (
            %a{:href => "#SSSa"}> SSSa
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#FSSa"} FSSa
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} gauge connection
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔢
                          %mn 8
                        %mo ⊕
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔢
                          %mn 8
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_i \in \Omega^1(U_i, \mathfrak{e}_8 \oplus \mathfrak{e}_8)
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+connection"} spin connection
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %mi 𝔰𝔬
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_i \in \Omega^1(U_i, \mathfrak{so})
                (the field of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
                in
                = succeed ");" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+order+formulation+of+gravity"} first order formulation of gravity
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mi B
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_B \in \Omega^2(U_i)
          %p
            which come with
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+strength"} field strength
            forms
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mi dR
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi i
                      %mo +
                      %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                        %mfrac
                          %mn 1
                          %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi i
                      %mo ∧
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_{A_i} = d_{dR} A_i + \tfrac{1}{2}[A_i \wedge A_i]
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi ω
                            %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mi dR
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mi i
                      %mo +
                      %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                        %mfrac
                          %mn 1
                          %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mi i
                      %mo ∧
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_{\omega_i} = d_{dR} \omega_i + \tfrac{1}{2}[\omega_i \wedge \omega_i]
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mi d
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mi i
                      %mo +
                      %mi CS
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo −
                      %mi CS
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_i = d B_i + CS(\omega_i) - CS(A_i)
                (
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                \-field strength shifted by the difference of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+forms"} Chern-Simons forms
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_i
                and
                = succeed ");" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ω
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_i
          %p
            satisfying the (twisted)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bianchi+identities"} Bianchi identities
            (
            %a{:href => "SSSa"}> SSSa
            ))
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mi dR
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mi i
                      %mo +
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi i
                      %mo ∧
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_{dR} F_{A_i} + [A_i \wedge F_{A_i}] = 0
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mi dR
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi ω
                            %mi i
                      %mo +
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mi i
                      %mo ∧
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi ω
                            %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_{dR} F_{\omega_i} + [\omega_i \wedge F_{\omega_i}] = 0
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mi dR
                      %mi H
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mi ω
                      %mo ∧
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mi ω
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mi A
                      %mo ∧
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_{dR} H = \langle F_\omega \wedge F_\omega \rangle  - \langle F_A \wedge F_A \rangle
          %p
            (together with more local cocycle components on higher overlaps). Notably the twisted Bianchi identity of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            exhibits the above cohomological identity in de Rham cocycles.
          %p
            These formulas characterize the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+mechanism"} Green-Schwarz anomaly cancellation conditions
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/background+gauge+field"} background gauge field
            content, that makes the heterotic string be well defined. Accordingly,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi String
                    %mi conn
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} String^{\mathbf{a}}_{conn}
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-groupoid"} smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+infinity-stack"} moduli 2-stack
            of anomaly free heterotic background fields (in the massless bosonic sector).
          %p
            Notice that if the twist
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %mover
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi gr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo −
                  %mover
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi gau
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tfrac{1}{2}\hat \mathbf{p_1}(\phi_{gr}) - \hat\mathbf{a}(\phi_{gau})
            happen to vanish (say because both the field of gravity and the gauge field are trivial), then the above homotopy pullback reduces to
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mn 2
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi conn
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi ϕ
                                  %mi B
                          %msub
                            %mo ⇙
                            %mo ≃
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mrow
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Ω
                            %mi cl
                            %mn 3
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ↪
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi ϕ
                                %mi C
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mn 3
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathbf{B}^2 U(1)_{conn}
                  \&amp;\to&amp;
                  *
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;{}^{\mathllap{\phi_B}}\swArrow_{\simeq}&amp;
                  \\downarrow^{}
                  \\\
                  \\Omega^3_{cl}(-) &amp; \stackrel{\phi_C}{\hookrightarrow} &amp; \mathbf{B}^3 U(1)_{conn}
                  }
          %p
            and exhibits
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_B
            as a genuine
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle+with+connection"} circle 2-bundle with connection
            (and its 3-form curvature
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            with
            = succeed ".)." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_B
            is a
            %em twisted
            circle 2-bundle, with the twist given by the “magnetic fivebrane current”
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi gr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo −
                    %mover
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi ga
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tfrac{1}{2}\hat \mathbf{p}_1(\phi_{gr}) - \hat \mathbf{a}(\phi_{ga})
          %h4#d_twisted_differential_fivebrane_structure__dual_greenschwarz_mechanism
            %strong d)
            Twisted differential Fivebrane structure – dual Green-Schwarz mechanism
          %p (…)
          %h3#HigherOrientifold
            %strong IV)
            Higher orientifold structure
          %h4#orientifolds Orientifolds
          %p
            An
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientifold"} orientifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
            for the bosonic string is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            or more generally
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            equipped with
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+cover"} double cover
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi w
                          %mi X
                        %mo :
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %msub
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w_X : X \to \mathbf{B} \mathbb{Z}_2
            %li
              %p
                a twisted
                = succeed "-equivariant" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mi B
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi Aut
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_B : X \to \mathbf{B}Aut(\mathbf{B}U(1))
                whose underlying double cover is
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi w
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
          %p
            This means that this background is a cocycle in
            = succeed "-twisted" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi w
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi Aut
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi J
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %msub
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathbf{B}U(1) &amp;\to&amp; \mathbf{B}Aut(\mathbf{B}U(1))
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathbf{J}}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}\mathbb{Z}_2
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            Hence the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            is now a cocycle in
            = succeed "-twisted" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi w
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %msub
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\phi_b \in \mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}\mathbb{Z}_2}( w_X , \mathbf{J})
                  \\,,
          %p
            or rather a differential refinement thereof. For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string"} string
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi φ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ν
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %msub
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi w
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\varphi, \nu) \in \mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}\mathbb{Z}_2}(\mathbf{w}_1(\Sigma), w_X)
                  \\,,
          %p
            given in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            by a diagram
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Σ
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi φ
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                    %mi w
                                  %mn 1
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mi ν
                          %msub
                            %mo ⇙
                            %mo ≃
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ↙
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi w
                                  %mi X
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %msub
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\Sigma &amp;&amp;\stackrel{\varphi}{\to}&amp;&amp; X
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{\mathbf{w}_1}}\searrow
                  \&amp;{}^{\nu}\swArrow_{\simeq}&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{w_X}}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}\mathbb{Z}_2
                  }
          %p consisting of
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a map
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi φ
                        %mo :
                        %mi Σ
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi : \Sigma \to X
            %li
              %p
                an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ν
                        %mo :
                        %msup
                          %mi φ
                          %mo *
                        %msub
                          %mi w
                          %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi w
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu : \varphi^* w_X \to \mathbf{w}_1(\Sigma)
          %h4#HWCompactifications Hořava-Witten compactifications
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ho%C5%99ava-Witten+theory"} Hořava-Witten theory
            there is similarly a twisted
            = succeed "-action" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} supergravity C-field
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mn 2
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi Aut
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mn 2
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi J
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %msub
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathbf{B}^2U(1) &amp;\to&amp; \mathbf{B}Aut(\mathbf{B}^2U(1))
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathbf{J}}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}\mathbb{Z}_2
                  }
                  \\,.
          %h3#further_twists Further twists
          %p There are various further twisted cohomological structures in string theory known or conjectured (for some of which possibly no smooth refinement has been constructed yet). We briefly list some of them.
          %h4#TwistedSuperBundle Twisted super bundle
          %p
            In work like
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Loop+Groups+and+Twisted+K-Theory"} Loop Groups and Twisted K-Theory
            the following structure plays a role:
          %p
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo :
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\epsilon : G \to \mathbb{Z}_2
          %p
            be a fixed group homomorphism. Then for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ⊕
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = E_0 \oplus E_1 \to X
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+bundle"} super vector bundle
            = succeed "-twist\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            such that an element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \in G
            acts by an even automorphism if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon(g)
            is even, and by an odd automorphism if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon(g)
            is odd (
            %a{:href => "#FreedLecture"}> Freed ESI lecture, (1.13)
            ).
          %p This is a special case of the general notion of twist discussed here by considering the canonical morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi Aut
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi e
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %msub
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathbf{B}Aut(E)
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow^{\mathbf{e}}
                  \\\
                  \\mathbf{B} \mathbb{Z}_2
                  }
          %p
            as the local coefficient bundle, and considering
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϵ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
            as the twist: then an
            = succeed "-twisting" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %msub
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}\mathbb{Z}_2}(\mathbf{B}\epsilon, \mathbf{e})
            given by a commuting triangle
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi G
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi Aut
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi B
                                %mi ϵ
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ↙
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi e
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %msub
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathbf{B}G &amp;&amp;\to&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}Aut(E)
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{\mathbf{B}\epsilon}}\searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{\mathbf{e}}}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}\mathbb{Z}_2
                  }
                  \\,.
          %h4#RelativeFields Relative fields
          %p
            Meanwhile in (
            %a{:href => "#FreedTeleman"}> Freed-Teleman 2012
            ) special cases of the general notion of
            %em twisted fields
            %a{:href => "#TableOfTwists"} above
            are being called
            = succeed "." do
              %em relative fields
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi π
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Grp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Grp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Smooth
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi \in Grp(Set) \hookrightarrow Grp(Smooth\infty Grpd)
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete group
            and for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo ¯
                  %mo ∈
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo ≔
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{X} \in \mathbf{H} \coloneqq
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
            any object (for instance a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo ¯
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo ¯
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_{\overline{X}} \colon \overline{X} \to \mathbf{B}\pi
            modulates a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to \overline{X}
            over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to \overline{X}
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
            map.
          %p
            Then the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twisted cohomology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo ¯
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}\pi}(-, \phi_{\overline{X}})
            has
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                domains are objects
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
                equipped with a
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi π
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mi Σ
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi Σ
                        %mo →
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi π
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_\Sigma \colon \Sigma \to \mathbf{B}\pi
            %li
              %p
                cocycles are morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mi Σ
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_\Sigma \to \phi_X
                in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} slice (∞,1)-topos
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi H
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi π
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}\pi}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagrams"} diagrams
                of the form
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi Σ
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mi f
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mi X
                                %mo ¯
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mrow
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi ϕ
                                      %mi Σ
                              %mo ↘
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mo ⇙
                                %mi θ
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mo ↙
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi ϕ
                                      %mi X
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mi π
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      \\Sigma &amp;&amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp;&amp; \overline{X}
                      \\\
                      \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{\phi_\Sigma}}\searrow &amp;\swArrow_{\theta}&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{\phi_X}}
                      \\\
                      \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}\pi
                      }
              %p
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi H
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo →
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon \Sigma \to \overline{X}
                equipped with equivalences
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi θ
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mi X
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mo ≃
                      %msub
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mi Σ
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\theta \colon f^* \phi_X \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} \phi_\Sigma
                      \\,.
          %p
            This class of examples is what appears as def. 3.4 in (
            %a{:href => "#FreedTeleman"}> Freed-Teleman
            ). It contains in particular the above examples of
            %em
              %a{:href => "#ReductionOfTheStructureGroup"} Reduction of structure group
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#SpinConnection"} its differential refinement
          %p
            Next, consider a compact Lie group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi G
                    %mo ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{G}
            and a central
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+extension"} group extension
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mo →
                    %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi \to G \to \overline{G}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi c
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mover
                    %mi G
                    %mo ¯
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 2
                  %mi π
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{c} \colon \mathbf{B}\overline{G} \to \mathbf{B}^2 \pi
                  \\,.
          %p
            Then the corresponding twisted cohomology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mn 2
                      %mi π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}^2 \pi}(-, \mathbf{c})
            has
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                domains are objects
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
                equipped with a
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi π
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}\pi
                = succeed "/" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-bundle"} principal 2-bundle
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+gerbe"} bundle gerbe
                modulated by a morphism
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mi Σ
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi Σ
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mn 2
                        %mi π
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_\Sigma \colon \Sigma \to \mathbf{B}^2 \pi
            %li
              %p
                cocycles are morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mi Σ
                      %mo →
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_\Sigma \to \mathbf{c}
                in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} slice (∞,1)-topos
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi H
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %msup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mn 2
                            %mi π
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}^2\pi}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagrams"} diagrams
                of the form
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi Σ
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mi f
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mi X
                                %mo ¯
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mrow
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi ϕ
                                      %mi Σ
                              %mo ↘
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mo ⇙
                                %mi θ
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mo ↙
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                    %mi c
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi B
                                %mn 2
                              %mi π
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      \\Sigma &amp;&amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp;&amp; \overline{X}
                      \\\
                      \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{\phi_\Sigma}}\searrow &amp;\swArrow_{\theta}&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{\mathbf{c}}}
                      \\\
                      \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}^2\pi
                      }
              %p
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi H
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo →
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon \Sigma \to \overline{X}
                equipped with equivalences
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi θ
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mo ≃
                      %msub
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\theta \colon \mathbf{c}(f) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} \phi_\Sigma
              %p
                between the principal 2-bundle/bundle gerbe
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{c}(f)
                induced by the
                = succeed "-principal" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi G
                          %mo ¯
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{G}
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mi Σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_\Sigma
          %p
            Alternatively one can use here the differential refinement of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mover
                    %mi G
                    %mo ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}\overline{G}
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo ¯
                    %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}\overline{G}_{conn}
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{G}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connections"} principal connections
          %p
            Examples and further details are discussed in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Schreiber"} Schreiber, section 7.1
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#FreedTeleman"} Freed-Teleman
          %h4#twisted_tmf Twisted tmf
          %ul
            %li
              twisted
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
              and charges for M5-branes (
              %a{:href => "#Ando-Sati"}> Ando-Sati
              ).
          %h4#twisted_morava_ktheory Twisted Morava K-theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                twisted
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morava+K-theory"} Morava K-theory
                (
                %a{:href => "#SatiWesterland"}> Sati-Westerland
                ).
            %li
              %p (…)
          %h2#LocalPrequantumFieldTheory
            %strong B)
            Local boundary prequantum field theory from twisted smooth cohomology
          %blockquote
            %p
              This section originates in some talk notes (
              %a{:href => "#SchreiberTwists2013"}> Schreiber, Twists 2013
              ).
          %p
            We indicate now how the twisted smooth cohomology data as in the examples above induces and in fact corresponds to data for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+field+theory"} prequantum field theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-models"} sigma-models
            %em localized
            (in the sense of the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+hypothesis"} cobordism hypothesis
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+prequantum+field+theory"} local prequantum field theory
            (
            %a{:href => "#lpqft"}> lpqft
            ).
          %p
            In order to formalize this accurately, we first talk a bit more about the relevant
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesion"} cohesion
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohesion"} differential cohesion
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+cohesion"} tangent cohesion
          %p
            In full generality,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            (see there for details) is what is given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categorical+hom-spaces"} (∞,1)-categorical hom-spaces
            in some
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-topos"} ∞-topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∈
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,A \in \mathbf{H}
            any two
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H(X,A) \coloneqq \pi_0 \mathbf{H}(X,A)
          %p
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            Therefore it is natural to ask:
            %em
              What is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
              to be like whose intrinsic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+cohomology"} equivariant
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twisted
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology"} stable
              = succeed "?" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
          %p
            And the answer we find is: it is to be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} tangent (∞,1)-topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \mathbf{H}
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
          %p
            For more on this see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+cohesion"} tangent cohesion
          %h3#cohesive_contexts_for_equivariant_differential_twisted_cohomology Cohesive contexts for equivariant differential twisted cohomology
          %p
            After the discovery of the role of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"} D-brane
            phenomena in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            involves various other
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twisted cohomology
            theories such as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morava+K-theory"} Morava K-theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Sati10"} Sati 10
          %p
            The suggestion that the right context for formulating the smooth and differential refinement of these twisted cohomology theories is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            We
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi H
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi Sh
                            %mn ∞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi SmthMfd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≃
                          %mi Funct
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi SmoothMfd
                            %mi op
                          %mo ,
                          %mi KanCplx
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mi stalkwise
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi homotopy
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi equivalences
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  \\mathbf{H}
                  \&amp;=
                  Sh_\infty(SmthMfd)
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \simeq
                  Funct(SmoothMfd^{op}, KanCplx)[\{stalkwise\;homotopy\;equivalences\}^{-1}]
                  \\end{aligned}
          %p
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stacks"} ∞-stacks
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            (the result of universally turning
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"} stalkwise
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalences"} homotopy equivalences
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaf"} presheaves of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complexes"} Kan complexes
            into actual
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalences"} homotopy equivalences
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Schreiber09"} Schreiber 09
          %p
            A full formalization of the classification of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundles"} principal ∞-bundles
            in such
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian cohomology
            was later given in (
            %a{:href => "#NSS"}> Nikolaus-Schreiber-Stevenson 12
            ). There it is shown that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Grp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \in Grp(\mathbf{H})
            an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"} ∞-group
            of twists, the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twisted cohomology
            is the plain cohomology of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} slice (∞,1)-topos
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Topos
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}G}  \;\; \in (\infty,1)Topos
                  \\,.
          %p
            Precisely, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho \in \mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{B}G}
            a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-action"} ∞-action
            on some
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            incarnated as its universal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} associated ∞-bundle
            (the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+coefficient+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} local coefficient ∞-bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi \colon X \longrightarrow \mathbf{B}G
            a twist, then the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twisted cohomology
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+coefficients"} local coefficients
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi χ
                    %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi ϕ
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi V
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi G
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi χ
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↙
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi ρ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi G
                    %mo }
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{H}_{\mathbf{B}G}(\chi_X,\rho)
                  \=
                  \\left\{
                  \\array{
                  X &amp;&amp; \stackrel{\phi}{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp; V//G
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{\chi}}\searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{\rho}}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}G
                  }
                  \\right\}
                  \\,.
          %p
            The observation that for the
            = succeed "-refinement" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twisted
            geometric cohomology it is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+quadruple"} adjoint quadruple
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functors"} (∞,1)-functors
            between
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} base (∞,1)-topos
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesion"}> cohesion
            ”)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %munder
                          %mo ←
                          %mi coDisc
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mi Γ
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi Disc
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi Π
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{H}
                  \\stackrel{\overset{\Pi}{\longrightarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{Disc}{\leftarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{\Gamma}{\longrightarrow}}{\underset{coDisc}{\leftarrow}}}}
                  \\infty Grpd
          %p
            (with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+object"} Disc
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codiscrete+object"} coDisc
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functors"} full and faithful (∞,1)-functors
            and the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+infinity-groupoid+of+a+locally+infinity-connected+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} fundamental ∞-groupoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization+of+cohesive+homotopy+types"} geometric realization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
            = succeed "-preserving)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-limit"} finite product
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "SatiSchreiberStasheff09"} Sati-Schreiber-Stasheff 09 (11)
          %p
            There it was shown that this serves to construct and characterize the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+differential+string+structures"} twisted differential string structures
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+differential+Fivebrane+structures"} twisted differential Fivebrane structures
            in (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+heterotic+string+theory"}> dual
            )
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
          %p
            A comprehensive theory of (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twisted
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+cohomology"} equivariant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
            formulated by just this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom"} axiom
            of “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesion"}> cohesion
            ” was then laid out in the thesis (
            %a{:href => "#Schreiber"}> Schreiber 11
            ). Parts of this appear in various articles, such as (
            %a{:href => "FiorenzaRogersSchreiber13"}> Fiorenza-Schreiber-Rogers 13
            ). See (Schreiber Synthetic 13eiberSynthetic)) for a fairly comprehensive survey.
          %p
            Notice that such
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesion"} cohesion
            is a very special property of some
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} (∞,1)-toposes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
            means that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+%E2%88%9E-connected+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} locally ∞-connected (∞,1)-topos
            and a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/globally+%E2%88%9E-connected+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} globally ∞-connected (∞,1)-topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi coDisc
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} coDisc
            means that it is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} local (∞,1)-topos
          %p
            Examples of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesion"} cohesive
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometry
            established and discussed in (
            %a{:href => "#Schreiber"}> Schreiber 11
            ) include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+topological+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} Euclidean topological ∞-groupoids
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Sh
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi TopMfd
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_\infty(TopMfd)
                is cohesive
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} smooth ∞-groupoids
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Sh
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi SmoothMfd
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_\infty(SmoothMfd)
                is cohesive
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} super ∞-groupoids
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Sh
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi SuperPoints
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_\infty(SuperPoints)
                is cohesive;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+super+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} smooth super ∞-groupoids
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Sh
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi SuperMfd
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_\infty(SuperMfd)
                is cohesive over
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} super ∞-groupoids
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+differential+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} synthetic differential ∞-groupoids
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Sh
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi FormalMfds
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_\infty(FormalMfds)
                is even “
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohesion"}> differentially cohesive
                ”, which allows to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom"} axiomatize
                also the notions of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+bundle"} jet bundle
                etc.;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+differential+super+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} synthetic differential super ∞-groupoids
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Sh
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi FormalSuperMfds
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_\infty(FormalSuperMfds)
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohesion"} differentially cohesive
                over
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} super ∞-groupoids
          %p
            Clearly these examples are all of a similar kind (modeled on variants of
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            categories which are usefully cohesive, for instance
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+objects"} simplicial objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}^{\Delta^{op}}
              is cohesive over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              (here
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
              of simplicial objects in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
          %p
            In October 2013
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Rezk"} Charles Rezk
            announced a new kind of cohesion, namely:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+equivariant+homotopy+theory"} global equivariant homotopy theory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Orb
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_\infty(Orb)
              (hence
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-presheaves
              on the global
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbit+category"} orbit category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
              produces
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotients"} homotopy quotients
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
              produces topological
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotients"} quotients
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+groups"} topological groups
              acting on
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
          %p
            But of course a central feature desireable for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+theory"} cohomology theory
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilization"} stabilization
            of cohesion/cohesive
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+objects"} spectrum objects
          %p
            In (
            %a{:href => "tangent+cohesion#BunkeNikolausVoelkl13"}> Bunke-Nikolaus-Völkl 2014
            ) is considered the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilization"} stabilization
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} smooth cohesion
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} stable (∞,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Stab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi SmthMfd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Stab(Sh_\infty(SmthMfd))
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+object"} spectrum object
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} smooth ∞-groupoids
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+quadruple"} adjoint quadruple
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+spectra"} (∞,1)-category of spectra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Stab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Spectra
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Stab(\infty Grpd) \simeq Spectra
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Stab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi SmthMfd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %munder
                          %mo ←
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi coDisc
                              %mi stab
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi Γ
                              %mi stab
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi Disc
                            %mi stab
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Π
                          %mi stab
                  %mi Spectra
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Stab(Sh_\infty(SmthMfd))
                  \\stackrel{\overset{\Pi^{stab}}{\longrightarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{Disc^{stab}}{\leftarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{\Gamma^{stab}}{\longrightarrow}}{\underset{coDisc^{stab}}{\leftarrow}}}}
                  Spectra
                  \\,.
          %p
            But this stable aspect is unified with the unstable cohesion by the notion of “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+cohesion"}> tangent cohesion
            ”. This we turn to now.
          %h3#cohesive_contexts_for_stable_twisted_cohomology Cohesive contexts for stable twisted cohomology
          %p
            We first discuss generally how the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} tangent (∞,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \mathbf{H}
            of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            is itself an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            over the tangent
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} base (∞,1)-topos
            (
            %a{:href => "#Joyal08"}> Joyal 08
            ). Then we observe that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \mathbf{H}
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesion"} cohesive
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            is and is in fact an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extension"} extension
            of the latter by its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilization"} stabilization
          %h4#tangent_topos
            Tangent
            = succeed "-topos" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi seq
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} seq
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              category as follows:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi seq
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %mo {
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mi ⋮
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mi ⋮
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi ⋯
                              %mtd
                                %mo →
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mi x
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi n
                                    %mo −
                                    %mn 1
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi p
                                      %mrow
                                        %mi n
                                        %mo −
                                        %mn 1
                              %mtd
                                %mo *
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mrow
                                  %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                    %mrow
                                      %msub
                                        %mi p
                                        %mrow
                                          %mi n
                                          %mo −
                                          %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mtd
                                %mo ⇙
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mrow
                                      %msub
                                        %mi i
                                        %mi n
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mo ↘
                                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} id
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo *
                              %mtd
