                    \\,.
          %h3#local_prequantum_field_theory Local prequantum field theory
          %p
            We describe the formulation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+prequantum+field+theory"} local prequantum field theory
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            (
            %a{:href => "#lpqft"}> lpqft
            ).
          %p
            A
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+field+theory"} classical field theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+field+theory"} prequantum field theory
            is traditionally defined by an
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+space"} smooth space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Fields
                    %mi traj
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Fields}_{traj}
            “of
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trajectories"} trajectories
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physical+system"} physical system
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi Fields
                            %mi traj
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mi exp
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi i
                                %mi S
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathbf{Fields}_{traj}
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\exp(i S)}}
                  \\\
                  U(1)
                  }
          %p
            to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            from this is to
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                choose a linearization in the form of the group
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⟶
                      %msub
                        %mi GL
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1) \longrightarrow GL_1(\mathbb{C})
                to the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+of+units"} group of units
                of the complex numbers,
            %li
              %p
                choose a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measure"} measure
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mi μ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d\mu
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi Fields
                        %mi traj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Fields}_{traj}
          %p
            and then declare that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral"} integral
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+integral"}> path integral
            ”)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi Fields
                        %mi traj
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi d
                  %mi μ
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\underset{\phi \in \mathbf{Fields}_{traj}}{\int} \exp(i S(\phi))\, d\mu \in \mathbb{C}
          %p
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+function"} partition function
            of the theory a kind of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/expectation+value"} expectation value
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probabilities"} probabilities
            replaced by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+amplitudes"} probability amplitudes
          %p
            In order to make sense of this (for a full discussion of “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivic+quantization"}> motivic quantization
            ” in this sense see (
            %a{:href => "#Nuiten13"}> Nuiten 13
            ), here we concentrate on the
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+field+theory"} pre-quantum aspects
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}U(1)
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+groupoid"} smooth
            universal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+U%281%29-bundles"} principal U(1)-bundles
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            as above is equivalently a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
