              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holography"} holographic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+field+theory"} boundary field theory
            way in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codimension"} codimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
            instead here in codimension
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            Accordingly, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+sections"} space of sections
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi
            is the higher
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+quantum+states"} space of quantum states
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codimension"} codimension
            0.
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} discrete ∞-groupoid
            then the space of sections has a particularly nice description, on which we focus for a bit:
          %p
            The space of co-sections is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-colimit"} (∞,1)-colimit
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mo •
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %munder
                    %mi lim
                    %mo →
                  %mi χ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi E
                  %mi Mod
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E_{\bullet + \chi}(X)
                  \\; \coloneqq\;
                  \\underset{\to}{\lim}
                  \\chi
                  \\;
                  \\in E Mod
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is also known as the
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi
              \-twisted
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectrum"} Thom spectrum
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (
            %a{:href => "#ABG"}> Ando-Blumberg-Gepner 10
            ).
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a map
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mrow
                          %mo •
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                          %mi χ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to E_{\bullet + \chi}(X)
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cycle"} cycle
                in
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi χ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twisted
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+homology"} generalized homology
                of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %li
              %p
                a map
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mrow
                          %mo •
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                          %mi χ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_{\bullet + \chi}(X) \to E
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
                in
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi χ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twisted
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+cohomology"} generalized cohomology
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %p Hence we write
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi E
                        %mrow
                          %mo •
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                          %mi χ
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mi X
                        %mo )
                      %mo ≔
                      %mrow
                        %mo [
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mrow
                            %mo •
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                            %mi χ
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %mi X
                          %mo )
                        %mo ,
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi E
                        %mo ]
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      E^{\bullet + \chi}\left(X\right)
                      \\coloneqq
                      \\left[
                      E_{\bullet + \chi}\left(X\right),
                      \\,
                      E
                      \\right]
                      \\,.
          %p
            Generally, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi χ
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_i \colon X_i \to E Mod
            two
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-module+bundles"} (∞,1)-module bundles
            over two spaces, a map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mo •
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %msub
                        %mi χ
                        %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mo •
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %msub
                        %mi χ
                        %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E_{\bullet + \chi_1}(X_1)
                  \\longrightarrow
                  E_{\bullet + \chi_2}(X_2)
          %p
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            in
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi χ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi χ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\chi_1, \chi_2)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twisted
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bivariant+cohomology"} bivariant
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
          %p
            Now given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+action+functional"} local action functional
            on a space of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trajectories"} trajectories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondence"} correspondence
            as above, this induces an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+kernel"} integral kernel
            for linear maps between sections of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+prequantum+line+bundles"} higher prequantum line bundles
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
