          %h3#cohesive_homotopy_type_theory Cohesive homotopy type theory
          %p
            In general the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
            encoded by an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            can be exotic. Two extra axioms ensure that it is modeled locally on
            = succeed "-connected" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+disks"} open disks
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean-topological+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} Euclidean-topological geometry
            and
            %em smooth open disks
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} smooth geometry
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bill+Lawvere"} Lawvere
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+homotopy+type+theory"} cohesive homotopy type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} interpreted
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} cohesive (∞,1)-toposes
          %h4#geometric_realization Geometric realization
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            is in particular equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} derived adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
            to the
            = succeed "-functor" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+constant+%E2%88%9E-stack"} locally constant ∞-stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Disc
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Disc
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Π
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi Disc
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo ↩
                      %mi Disc
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi Π
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\Pi \dashv Disc)
                  \:
                  \\mathbf{H}
                  \\stackrel{\overset{\Pi}{\to}}{\underset{Disc}{\hookleftarrow}}
                  \\infty Grpd
                  \\,.
          %p
            We may think of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
            as being the functor that sends a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} smooth ∞-groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+infinity-groupoid+in+a+locally+infinity-connected+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} fundamental path ∞-groupoid
          %p
            Under the identification (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+hypothesis"} homotopy hypothesis theorem
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\infty Grpd \stackrel{{\vert-\vert}}{\to} Top
          %p
            this identifies with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
            of geometric homotopy types /
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stacks"} ∞-stacks
          %p
            We say that a lift of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            through
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
            is a
            %strong geometric refinement
            of the diagram.
          %h4#differential_cohomology Differential cohomology
          %p
            Write
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Π
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi Disc
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi Π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\Pi} \coloneqq Disc \circ \Pi
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ♭
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi Disc
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat \coloneqq Disc \circ \Gamma
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"} ∞-group
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                    %mo ♭
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat_{dR} \mathbf{B}G \coloneqq * \times_{\mathbf{B}G} \flat \mathbf{B}G
            %em de Rham coefficient object
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
          %p
            There is a canonical morphism
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi θ
                    %mo :
                    %mi G
