          %h2#RelatedEntries Related entries
          %p An entry with discussion of and list of examples of twisted differential structures is
          %ul
            %li
              %em>
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+differential+c-structures"} twisted differential c-structures
              \.
          %p Related expositions include the following:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics"} geometry of physics
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundles+in+physics"} fiber bundles in physics
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory+FAQ"} string theory FAQ
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+smooth+cohomology+in+string+theory"} twisted smooth cohomology in string theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motives+in+physics"} motives in physics
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert%27s+sixth+problem"} Hilbert's sixth problem
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+theory+and+physics"} model theory and physics
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-infinity+algebras+in+physics"} L-infinity algebras in physics
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivation+for+sheaves%2C+cohomology+and+higher+stacks"} motivation for sheaves, cohomology and higher stacks
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/applications+of+%28higher%29+category+theory"} applications of (higher) category theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivation+for+higher+differential+geometry"} motivation for higher differential geometry
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivation+for+cohesion"} motivation for cohesion
          %h2#References References
          %p
            The string-theoretic aspects of the above discussion owe a lot to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Geometric+and+topological+structures+related+to+M-branes"} Geometric and topological structures related to M-branes
              , part I (
              %a{:href => "http://arXiv.org/abs/1001.5020"}> arXiv:1001.5020
              ), part
              %em
                II: Twisted
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi String
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} String
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi String
                        %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} String^c
                structures
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv/1007.5419"}> arXiv:1007.5419
              ); part
              %em III: Twisted higher structures
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1008.1755"}> arXiv:1008.1755
              )
          %p
            The notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twisted cohomology
            by sections of twisting coeffcient
            = succeed "-bundles" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %ul#ABG
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthew+Ando"}> Matthew Ando
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Blumberg"} Andrew Blumberg
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Gepner"} David Gepner
              = succeed "," do
                %em Twists of K-theory and TMF
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Rosenberg"} Jonathan Rosenberg
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Superstrings, Geometry, Topology, and
                  = succeed "-algebras" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mo *
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^*
              %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/bookstore-getitem/item=PSPUM-81"} vol 81
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1002.3004"}> arXiv:1002.3004
              )
          %p
            but considered in the non-stable context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian cohomology
            and refined from bare homotopy types to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+homotopy+type+theory"} geometric homotopy types
          %p
            The fundamental observation that background gauge fields in string theory are modeled by (twisted)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
            goes back to
          %ul#Freed
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Freed"}> Dan Freed
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+charge+quantization+and+generalized+differential+cohomology"} Dirac charge quantization and generalized differential cohomology
          %p
            and literature referenced there. For this classical literature, notably on the example of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+K-theory"} twisted
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+K-theory"} differential
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientifolds"} orientifolds
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Freed"}> Dan Freed
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em K-Theory in Quantum Field Theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math-ph/0206031"} arXiv:math-ph/0206031
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+dimensional+Chern-Simons+theory"} 7d Chern-Simons theory
            that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} supergravity C-field
            participates in, the relation of the flux quantization to the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+principle"} holographic
            description of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-dual+higher+gauge+field"} self-dual
            field on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            has been discussed in
          %ul#Witten96
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              ,
              %em Five-Brane Effective Action In M-Theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9610234"}> arXiv:hep-th/9610234
              )
          %ul#Witten96b
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em On Flux Quantization In M-Theory And The Effective Action
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9609122"} arXiv:hep-th/9609122
          %p A precise mathematical formulation of the proposal made there is given in
          %ul#HopkinsSinger
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Hopkins"}> Mike Hopkins
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isadore+Singer"} Isadore Singer
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quadratic+Functions+in+Geometry%2C+Topology%2C+and+M-Theory"} Quadratic Functions in Geometry, Topology, and M-Theory
          %p
            in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quadratic+refinement"} quadratic refinement
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/secondary+intersection+pairing"} secondary intersection pairing
            via
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+integral+Wu+structures"} differential integral Wu structures
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
          %p
            The suggestion that it is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stack+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} ∞-stack (∞,1)-topos
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            which is the right context for studying the twisted differential smooth cohomology in string theory was made in
          %ul#Schreiber09
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Background+fields+in+twisted+differential+nonabelian+cohomology"} Background fields in twisted differential nonabelian cohomology
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Oberwolfach+Workshop%2C+June+2009+--+Strings%2C+Fields%2C+Topology"} Oberwolfach Workshop, June 2009 – Strings, Fields, Topology
          %p
            The smooth
            = succeed "-stack" do
