              at
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://maths-old.anu.edu.au/esi/2012/"} ESI Program on K-Theory and Quantum Fields
              (2012) (
              %a{:href => "http://www.ma.utexas.edu/users/dafr/ESI.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            Later, some special cases of the general notion of twisted fields considered
            %a{:href => "#TableOfTwists"} above
            are being called
            %em relative fields
            in
          %ul#FreedTeleman
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Constantin+Teleman"} Constantin Teleman
              %em Relative quantum field theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1212.1692"}> arXiv:1212.1692
              )
          %p
            as discussed above in the section
            %em
              %a{:href => "#RelativeFields"} Relative fields
            \.
